        {
          "id": "a4d92464-01f2-4d6c-a3c8-63fdd4ae3540",
          "course_id": "60070fd5-e847-46d2-8786-94c8022f8682",
          "title": "Introduction to Polynomials",
          "content": null,
          "lesson_order": 5,
          "created_at": "2025-09-10T14:00:59.317226+00:00",
          "is_preview": false,
          "slug": "polynomial-intro",
          "content_html": "<h3>Introduction to Polynomials</h3>\n<p>A polynomial is an algebraic expression consisting of variables and coefficients, involving only addition, subtraction, multiplication, and non-negative integer exponents.</p>\n<h4>Components of a Polynomial:</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Terms:</strong> Individual parts separated by + or -</li>\n<li><strong>Coefficients:</strong> Numerical factors of variables</li>\n<li><strong>Variables:</strong> Letters representing unknown values</li>\n<li><strong>Degree:</strong> Highest power of the variable</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Types of Polynomials:</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Monomial:</strong> Single term (e.g., 3x)</li>\n<li><strong>Binomial:</strong> Two terms (e.g., 2x + 5)</li>\n<li><strong>Trinomial:</strong> Three terms (e.g., x² + 3x + 2)</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Examples:</h4>\n<p>• 2x³ + 5x² - 3x + 1 (degree 3)</p>\n<p>• 4x² - 7x + 2 (degree 2)</p>\n<p>• 3x + 5 (degree 1)</p>",
          "content_text": null,
          "content_type": "html"
        },
        {
          "id": "f8e33eaa-0327-47c7-866c-d0cddc568291",
          "course_id": "492e363b-423c-4467-96fd-a89abafa5017",
